  "changed_since_previous": "Now provides the full patch including the P2A input exemption logic in IsWitnessStandard, unit tests in transaction_tests.cpp, and functional test coverage in feature_taproot.py.",
  "card": "Relaxes mempool policy to treat Taproot annexes as standard if they consist solely of the 0x50 marker or unstructured data starting with 0x50 0x00. Under current policy, any Taproot transaction with an annex is rejected from standard mempools. To protect multi-party transactions against unilateral witness inflation or pinning, the rule requires all non-P2A inputs in a transaction to include an annex if any input does. The PR revisits the concept from closed PR 27926 and Libre Relay without citing new external user requirements.",
